3:This project is being developed for the **NeatLogs Hackathon**.
7:> **Build an AI agent that completes a substantial real-world task from start to finish, using neatlogs to trace and improve its runs and Entire to capture coding context and checkpoints, with other partner tools as optional enhancements.**
11:WhatsApp messages go to the **Assistant**, the primary orchestrator. It handles general conversation directly and delegates company and market research to the **Market Researcher**, which owns the Crustdata company search, enrichment, and web search tools. Business financial analysis goes to the **CFO Agent**, which analyzes figures supplied in the conversation, including cash flow, runway, budgets, pricing, and hiring scenarios. For combined requests, the Assistant passes market research findings to the CFO Agent and synthesizes the final reply. GitHub questions (repositories, issues, pull requests, Actions runs) go to a read-only copy of the **GitHub Agent**.
15:The **GitHub Agent** connects to GitHub's official remote MCP server (repos, issues, pull requests, Actions, account context) using `GITHUB_PAT`. In the web chat it can also make changes, but every tool the server does not mark read-only (`readOnlyHint: true`) pauses for an inline Approve/Deny card; a denied call never runs, and sending a new message drops any approval left unanswered. The Assistant (and therefore WhatsApp) only ever gets its read-only tools, so it cannot write to GitHub. Without `GITHUB_PAT` the agent starts with no tools.
23:Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in the provider and integration credentials. For the GitHub Agent, set `GITHUB_PAT` to a fine-grained personal access token scoped to the repositories it may use (read/write on Contents, Issues, Pull requests and Actions for changes; read-only permissions are enough for inspection).
46:- **NeatLogs**: All Mastra agents are wrapped with `neatlogs/mastra`, recording agent runs, model steps, tool calls, inputs/outputs, timing, token usage when returned, and errors. CLI and WhatsApp runs have request traces; WhatsApp also records history message count/bytes and reply delivery. Tracing does not trim model context.
47:- **GitHub MCP**: The GitHub Agent uses GitHub's hosted MCP server (`https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/`) through `@mastra/mcp`, limited to the context, repos, issues, pull_requests and actions toolsets.
50:## View Neatlogs traces
52:Set `NEATLOGS_API_KEY` in `.env` to your Neatlogs project ingest key, then restart `npm run bot` (or run `npm start -- "Say hello in one sentence"`). Optional `NEATLOGS_ENDPOINT` selects the ingest endpoint; `NEATLOGS_DEBUG=true` enables SDK diagnostics. Without a key, dashboard export is disabled and startup prints a warning.
54:Open https://app.neatlogs.com and select the project matching your key. Open its traces view and find the `whatsapp.request` or `cli.request` run. The terminal prints the exact `traceId` for each request; use it to identify the run. Expand the agent/model/tool spans to inspect each step. WhatsApp turns share a hashed conversation session ID. Agent/model/tool tracing captures conversation content and tool results; session hashing only hides the phone number in the session identifier.
